      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "<b>Perennial river:</b>a river that flows continuously throughout the
    year, even during dry seasons. These rivers are typically sourced by a combination
    of rainfall, melting snow, and groundwater. It consists of three major parts-
    Glacial Origin (near the river\u2019s source in the Himalayas), the Snow-Fed
    River Body and the entire course through glacier melting.  \r\n\r\n\r\n"
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
